# The combined command, folded by the line wrap

The case #1905 lost between review rounds, and the reason this directory exists.

The payload is `memory/workflow/review/memory.md` as it stood at `2826a660` —
the exact bytes that PR set out to remove. The two flags sit in one inline code
span, and the span crosses a source line, because the combined command is 82
characters and this repository wraps prose at ~82.

Round 1 of that review folded newlines and caught it. Round 2 rewrote the check
to stop depending on the `gh pr edit` prefix, dropped the fold in the same edit,
and went from 1 hit to 0 on this input. Nothing failed. Round 2's reviewer found
it by hand.

A guard that judges one source line at a time cannot see this: neither line
carries both flags.
